{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794735262,"nonce":"DQiubV6RYsQzy98/zXKJuJe1UUc=","title":"An hxn package cannot carry hand-written Haxe or extra extraParams.hxml lines","message":"`hxn package` writes the haxelib from generated classes alone, and `extraParams.hxml` with only `--macro hxn.Bind.lib(...)`; a library's CI checks the committed copies against generation. A driver library such as hxn-gpu-metal needs Haxe of its own beside the binding: an hxnsl target (a macro that compiles the shader's MSL to a metallib with `xcrun metal` during the build) and the init macro that registers it for the driver's shader family. Today that can only live in hxnsl itself or in a second haxelib.\n\nA setting under `[package.metadata.hxn]` naming a directory of Haxe sources to include in the package's class path, and init macros to add to `extraParams.hxml`, would cover it, with `hxn package` and the generated-files check treating them as sources rather than generated output.","files":null}]}